ypotheses satisfy all three new assertions identically because the chosen inputs never diverge by more than 1 cent from the threshold, so no assertion distinguishes a percentage-based rate from a fixed-amount discount.","No test in this diff uses a subtotal materially larger than the threshold (e.g. an order well above 10_000) that would separate the two hypotheses."],"behavioral_consequence":"A future change that alters the discount mechanism (e.g. from a 10% rate to a fixed 1,000-cent deduction, or to a different percentage that happens to align near the threshold) or that miscalculates the discount for larger orders will pass all three of these tests undetected, giving false confidence that the bulk-discount calculation is correctly validated when in fact only its on/off boundary is proven."},{"finding_id":"boundary-tests-omit-vip-tier-interaction","severity":"WARNING","cluster_ids":["cluster:fbcffac32de17df26fcb836f"],"provenance":[{"cluster_id":"cluster:fbcffac32de17df26fcb836f","evidence_id":"diff:f343ecb7f4e6c9ce1ce085f1","path":"src/test/java/com/sweforge/pricing/PricingCalculatorTest.java","start_line":18,"end_line":33,"hunk_identity":"@@ -18,4 +18,16 @@ class PricingCalculatorTest {"}],"concise_summary":"The three new threshold-boundary tests all construct Order with the single-argument constructor (no CustomerTier), so they only validate bulk-discount boundary behavior for the default tier. No new or existing test in this diff exercises the subtotal threshold boundary together with CustomerTier.VIP, leaving discount-stacking/interaction behavior at the boundary unproven.","concrete_source_facts":["subtotalJustBelowThresholdHasNoDiscount, subtotalAtThresholdGetsBulkDiscount, and subtotalJustAboveThresholdGetsBulkDiscount all call `new Order(List.of(new Item(...)))` with no CustomerTier argument.","The pre-existing adjacent test vipOrderGetsVipDiscount uses the two-argument constructor `new Order(List.of(...), CustomerTier.VIP)` but with items totaling 6_000 cents, well below the 10_000-cent bulk threshold, so it does not cross the boundary.","No test in this diff combines a VIP-tier customer with a subtotal at or near the 10_000-cent bulk-discount threshold."],"behavioral_consequence":"If bulk and tier discounts are meant to stack, cap, or take precedence in a specific order near the threshold, a regression in that interaction logic (e.g. double-applying discounts, or VIP discount masking/being masked by the bulk discount) would not be caught by any test in this diff."}],"failure_reason":"","failure_stage":"NONE","rejected_findings":[],"prompt_chars":3980,"provider_requests":1},"candidate_associations":[{"finding_id":"boundary-tests-do-not-disambiguate-discount-mechanism","candidate_requirement_ids":[],"basis":"NONE","exact_range_requirement_ids":[],"same_hunk_requirement_ids":[],"same_catalog_requirement_ids":[],"same_path_requirement_ids":[],"basis_scope":"NONE","primary_exact_range_requirement_ids":[],"context_exact_range_requirement_ids":[],"primary_same_hunk_requirement_ids":[],"context_same_hunk_requirement_ids":[]},{"finding_id":"boundary-tests-omit-vip-tier-interaction","candidate_requirement_ids":[],"basis":"NONE","exact_range_requirement_ids":[],"same_hunk_requirement_ids":[],"same_catalog_requirement_ids":[],"same_path_requirement_ids":[],"basis_scope":"NONE","primary_exact_range_requirement_ids":[],"context_exact_range_requirement_ids":[],"primary_same_hunk_requirement_ids":[],"context_same_hunk_requirement_ids":[]}]}
